---
description: Data ownership and TanStack Query conventions
globs: ["app/**/*.ts", "app/**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: true
---

See docs/DATA_OWNERSHIP.md and docs/QUERY_CONVENTIONS.md.

- Mutable backend state → TanStack Query. Route loaders → build-time public
  content only. `useState` → ephemeral UI state.
- Never use `clientLoader` and TanStack Query for the same mutable domain.
- Never put backend entities in Zustand/Redux. Never add a second HTTP client.
- Never use `useEffect` + `fetch` for server data.
- All network calls go through `app/lib/api/client.ts`.
- All query keys come from `app/lib/api/query-keys.ts`.
- Never retry a 4xx. "Class full" is an answer, not a failure.
- Transactions against a session balance are never optimistic.
- Do not re-implement backend rules. Render `eligibility`, `cancellation` and
  `waitlistAutoPromote` as returned; map codes to copy, and always produce a
  sentence for an unknown code.
- Do not call `Date.now()` during render; anchor to `query.dataUpdatedAt`.
- Every remote surface designs loading, empty, error and stale states.
